                                "sense_id": "abec6df9-cb8d-3741-bb9c-2e5fab12ebd4",
                                "text": "2004: The synchrocyclotron was able to accelerate protons to sufficient energies that collisions with nuclei produce pions, the lightest particles that, we now know, are made from a single quark and an antiquark. — Frank Close, Particle Physics: A Very Short Introduction (Oxford 2004, p. 50)"
                            }
                        ]
